            <ArticleTitle>Coronary revascularization--2009: state of the art.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.semtcvs.2009.08.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite advances in percutaneous coronary intervention, coronary artery bypass grafting remains the most effective intervention for complex coronary artery disease in survival, freedom from reintervention, and cost-effectiveness. To ensure that patients have access to this &quot;gold-standard&quot; treatment, a multidisciplinary team approach, rather than an individual cardiologist acting as a &quot;gatekeeper,&quot; should be the standard of care when intervention is necessary, to ensure transparency, real patient choice, and genuine informed consent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
